=== harnez 
Manage Claude Code, Prime Agent, and other agent harnesses from a YAML definition

Usage:
  harnez [command]

Available Commands:
  agent           Manage subagent sessions
  agent-collector Run the local server and usage collector (compatibility alias for server)
  agy-statusline  Render or manage the Antigravity CLI context and quota status line
  apply           Apply config.yaml to global Claude Code and agent harness directories
  assess          Fast code/doc metrics, token estimation, and repository feasibility report
  channel         Serve the opt-in local Claude MCP channel canary
  clean           Remove stale process records and release verified quota-1 state
  compact         Verbatim transcript compaction powered by decision models (Jev)
  compact-check   Assess whether a /compact likely dropped information (manual, opt-in)
  completion      Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  compose         Print a ready-to-use snippet from the embedded spec
  config          Get, set or unset keys of .harnez/repo.yaml, like git config
  decide          Ask a decision model (Jev) typed questions: noul, choice, score
  diff            Show what apply would change in managed blocks
  distill         Strip low-signal noise (passing tests, ANSI, repeats) from command output
  dochistory      Analyze Git document and multi-track repository evolution history
  docs            Project-scoped operations on already-installed copyable docs
  exec            Run a command, proxy its stdio unbuffered, and record shell-call telemetry
  feedback        Record and review agent-observed harnez bugs and instruction gaps
  find            Query repository-data entities with a short fuzzy-text/filter grammar
  guard           Rule enforcer and safety guardrail commands
  help            Help about any command
  index           Regenerate issue indexes and docs/README.md's studies table from source files
  init            Set up a project directory with AGENTS.md, language docs, and Makefile targets
  install         Install an optional dependency and run its bootstrap
  issues          Change a ticket's Status line, resync issue indexes, and commit -- in one call
  lint            Check files against harnez repository rules and conventions
  log             Show harnez's own CLI invocation history, newest first (git log for harnez)
  man             Generate, print, or install roff man pages
  mcp             Serve Harnez agent tools over MCP stdio
  mode            Switch ConciseMode terseness level and synchronize .harnez/rules/Local.md
  rate            Record a 1-5 quality rating for an internal tool call, or a lean --ok heartbeat
  read            Read bounded text or explicitly requested visual PNG cards
  release         Language-agnostic version bump, build, minisign, and forge publish pipeline
  repo-history    Multi-track Git history evolution sparks across code, tests, docs, skills, and issues
  repo-status     Brief, quiet-by-default summary of git working-tree state
  revert          Revert managed configuration or one-off changes
  scan-docs       Scan immediate child agent projects for managed-docs drift
  server          Run Harnez local services
  session         Extract retrospective evidence from local Claude Code sessions
  skill           Install, search, and explore external agent skills from git repositories
  skills          Inspect and export Harnez's built-in skill catalogue
  stats           Report call frequency, average score, failure rate, and byte savings from tool_calls telemetry
  status          Show config summary and applied state
  statusline      Render context and usage data for Claude Code or Antigravity CLI
  subagent        Stage provider-aware subagent context and optionally run a launcher
  tui             Interactive Loom-based terminal chat interface for harnez
  usage           Show unified token, session, and quota status across AI coding agents

Flags:
  -h, --help      help for harnez
  -v, --version   version for harnez

Use "harnez [command] --help" for more information about a command.

=== harnez agent
Manage subagent sessions across supported providers.

Short forms:
  harnez agent -p "summarise the open tickets"
  harnez agent "update the changelog"
  harnez agent --name docs -d ~/projects/x "update the changelog"
  harnez agent -c -p "continue"
  harnez agent start --name w --model luna -f task.md -- "extra instructions"
  harnez agent start -i --model claude:haiku --name chat
  harnez agent resume --name w "next step"
  harnez agent resume -i --name w
  harnez agent --name w -p "/compact"
  harnez agent --model luna:low --role advisor -p "how does X work?"

Models: run "harnez agent models" for the known names. --model takes
provider:name[:tier], a short alias (luna, opus) or alias:tier (luna:low).
The model default comes from spec/agent.yaml. Agents run with -d <dir> as their
working directory (default: cwd); resume reuses the session's directory.
Sessions are chosen by --name, attribution in -d, or -c. Use -- to send text
literally. Slash commands are /compact, /stop, and /status. Automatic compaction uses
agent.compact_thresholds from ~/.harnez/config.yaml, then spec model defaults,
then user agent.compact_threshold_tokens, then the spec global default.

Usage:
  harnez agent [flags]
  harnez agent [command]

Available Commands:
  compact     Compact an agent session
  delete      Delete an agent session
  disable     Set subagent dispatch policy to native
  enable      Set subagent dispatch policy to harnez
  list        List agent sessions
  models      List known agent models with roles and when to use them
  rate        Rate the latest turn of an agent session
  resume      Resume an existing agent session
  selftest    Run agent background task execution self-test
  send        Send to a live session or queue for an exec worker
  start       Start a new agent session
  status      Show agent session status
  stop        Stop an agent session
  wait        Wait for an agent session to finish

Flags:
      --allow-exhausted-quota   start even when cached provider quota is exhausted
  -c, --continue                resume the most recently active attributable session
  -d, --dir string              agent working directory (all providers) and session scope (default ".")
  -f, --file strings            prompt file (repeatable; - reads stdin)
  -h, --help                    help for agent
      --json                    JSON output
      --model string            provider:model[:tier]
      --name string             session name
      --plan string             planning gate: yes or no (default "no")
  -p, --prompt string           prompt text
      --role string             agent role for a new session (default from spec/agent.yaml); roles:
                                  advisor (aliases: arch, auditor, explorer, planner, scout, search): Research the code and return a concise read-only plan.
                                  developer (aliases: coder, dev, implementer, worker): Implement assigned work, run checks, and commit the result.
                                  orchestrator (aliases: coordinator, lead): Coordinate work and delegate to leaf workers.
                                  reviewer (aliases: checker, critic, review): Inspect changes and report actionable findings without editing.
      --store-dir string        session store directory (default "$HOME/.harnez/agents")
      --stream string           live output: full (all messages) or stats (heartbeats and final reply only) (default "full")
      --timeout duration        maximum foreground turn duration (0 waits without a limit)

Use "harnez agent [command] --help" for more information about a command.

