=== harnez agent resume
Resume an existing agent session.

Run workers in your session background, not the machine background.
Session background: a job owned by your chat session; it shows in your task
list and its exit wakes you. Machine background (shell &, nohup, setsid):
invisible to you, so you could only find out by polling. No external event
system will notify you; your own background tool is the only signal.

One call per worker, with HTO=0 so the turn never detaches after 60s:
  Claude Code  Bash tool, run_in_background: true, command
               "HTO=0 harnez agent start ...". Its exit sends you a
               task-notification. Claude Code stops background jobs after
               30 minutes: size each worker turn to finish before that.
  run_in_background: Claude Code Bash tool parameter only; not a harnez flag.
  AGY          run_command with "HTO=0 harnez agent start ..." and a small
               WaitMsBeforeAsync (e.g. 500); you are notified on completion.
  Codex        exec_command with "HTO=0 harnez agent start ..."; then call
               write_stdin on the returned session_id with chars "" until
               it reports an exit code.

Then tell the user the job id and the session name. Claude Code and AGY: end
your turn or do other work until notified. Codex: keep calling write_stdin
until the exit code. Never check status or logs in a loop while the job runs.
Use "harnez agent wait <session>" only to recover a lost job.

Usage:
  harnez agent resume [session] [prompt...] [flags]

Examples:
  harnez agent resume --name w "next step"
  harnez agent resume <id> "next step"
  harnez agent resume -i --name w

Flags:
  -c, --continue                resume the most recently active attributable session
  -f, --file strings            prompt file (repeatable; - reads stdin)
  -h, --help                    help for resume
  -i, --interactive             resume in the provider's interactive terminal
      --json                    JSON output
      --plan string             planning gate: yes or no (default "no")
  -p, --prompt string           prompt text
      --stream string           live output: full (all messages) or stats (heartbeats and final reply only) (default "full")
      --worker-session string   internal detached worker session ID

Global Flags:
      --allow-exhausted-quota   start even when cached provider quota is exhausted
  -d, --dir string              agent working directory (all providers) and session scope (default ".")
      --model string            provider:model[:tier]
      --name string             session name
      --role string             agent role for a new session (default from spec/agent.yaml); roles:
                                  advisor (aliases: arch, auditor, explorer, planner, scout, search): Research the code and return a concise read-only plan.
                                  developer (aliases: coder, dev, implementer, worker): Implement assigned work, run checks, and commit the result.
                                  orchestrator (aliases: coordinator, lead): Coordinate work and delegate to leaf workers.
                                  reviewer (aliases: checker, critic, review): Inspect changes and report actionable findings without editing.
      --store-dir string        session store directory (default "$HOME/.harnez/agents")
      --timeout duration        maximum foreground turn duration (0 waits without a limit)

=== harnez agent selftest
Run agent background task execution self-test.
Run with --step hello to begin.

=== harnez agent send
Send to a live Claude channel, Codex session, or supervised AGY session by --name or --id. The message is the positional argument; -m/--message and -p/--prompt are accepted alternatives. Without a target, send lists the names of live sessions. AGY messages queue until the supervised session is idle. Only Claude supports --wait for optional receipt confirmation, which does not confirm task completion. If no live route matches, an exact registry exec session in --store-dir receives a durable queue message for its next explicit resume. Resumable completed sessions can receive queued messages; deleted, blocked, or non-resumable sessions cannot. Batch workers consume the queue on resume only, not during a running turn.

Usage:
  harnez agent send (--name <session> | --id <session-id>) <message> [flags]

Examples:
  harnez agent send --name harnez-53ih "look at ticket 748 in harnez"
  harnez agent send --name agy-worker "please review this"
  harnez agent send --id 86443124-b692-49e4-ae92-942b0177664f --wait "please confirm"

Flags:
  -h, --help               help for send
      --id string          Claude, Codex, or AGY session ID
  -m, --message string     message text (alternative to the positional message)
  -p, --prompt string      message text (alternative to the positional message)
      --timeout duration   positive receipt wait timeout (default from spec/channel.yaml)
      --wait               wait for optional Claude receipt confirmation

Global Flags:
      --allow-exhausted-quota   start even when cached provider quota is exhausted
  -d, --dir string              agent working directory (all providers) and session scope (default ".")
      --model string            provider:model[:tier]
      --name string             session name
      --role string             agent role for a new session (default from spec/agent.yaml); roles:
                                  advisor (aliases: arch, auditor, explorer, planner, scout, search): Research the code and return a concise read-only plan.
                                  developer (aliases: coder, dev, implementer, worker): Implement assigned work, run checks, and commit the result.
                                  orchestrator (aliases: coordinator, lead): Coordinate work and delegate to leaf workers.
                                  reviewer (aliases: checker, critic, review): Inspect changes and report actionable findings without editing.
      --store-dir string        session store directory (default "$HOME/.harnez/agents")

=== harnez agent start
Start a new agent session. A leading role or alias may be positional; add a session name before the prompt when needed.

Run workers in your session background, not the machine background.
Session background: a job owned by your chat session; it shows in your task
list and its exit wakes you. Machine background (shell &, nohup, setsid):
invisible to you, so you could only find out by polling. No external event
system will notify you; your own background tool is the only signal.

One call per worker, with HTO=0 so the turn never detaches after 60s:
  Claude Code  Bash tool, run_in_background: true, command
               "HTO=0 harnez agent start ...". Its exit sends you a
               task-notification. Claude Code stops background jobs after
               30 minutes: size each worker turn to finish before that.
  run_in_background: Claude Code Bash tool parameter only; not a harnez flag.
  AGY          run_command with "HTO=0 harnez agent start ..." and a small
               WaitMsBeforeAsync (e.g. 500); you are notified on completion.
  Codex        exec_command with "HTO=0 harnez agent start ..."; then call
               write_stdin on the returned session_id with chars "" until
               it reports an exit code.

Then tell the user the job id and the session name. Claude Code and AGY: end
your turn or do other work until notified. Codex: keep calling write_stdin
until the exit code. Never check status or logs in a loop while the job runs.
Use "harnez agent wait <session>" only to recover a lost job.

Usage:
  harnez agent start [role] [name] [prompt...] [flags]

Examples:
  harnez agent start --name w --model luna -f task.md -- "extra instructions"
  harnez agent start explorer "audit SQLite queries"
  harnez agent start coder my-worker "implement ticket 041"
  harnez agent start -i --model claude:haiku --name chat

Flags:
      --allow-exhausted-quota   start even when cached provider quota is exhausted
  -f, --file strings            prompt file (repeatable; - reads stdin)
  -h, --help                    help for start
  -i, --interactive             launch the provider's interactive terminal
      --json                    JSON output
      --plan string             planning gate: yes or no (default "no")
  -p, --prompt string           prompt text
      --stream string           live output: full (all messages) or stats (heartbeats and final reply only) (default "full")
      --worker-session string   internal detached worker session ID

Global Flags:
  -d, --dir string         agent working directory (all providers) and session scope (default ".")
      --model string       provider:model[:tier]
      --name string        session name
      --role string        agent role for a new session (default from spec/agent.yaml); roles:
                             advisor (aliases: arch, auditor, explorer, planner, scout, search): Research the code and return a concise read-only plan.
                             developer (aliases: coder, dev, implementer, worker): Implement assigned work, run checks, and commit the result.
                             orchestrator (aliases: coordinator, lead): Coordinate work and delegate to leaf workers.
                             reviewer (aliases: checker, critic, review): Inspect changes and report actionable findings without editing.
      --store-dir string   session store directory (default "$HOME/.harnez/agents")
      --timeout duration   maximum foreground turn duration (0 waits without a limit)

