=== harnez bench
Send small specced tasks to agent CLIs under a documentation condition
(lite/full docs, with or without PNG cards) and record scored results in a bench
database (~/.harnez/bench/bench.sqlite) that is separate from telemetry.

The feature is opt-in: run 'harnez bench --setup' once, then use 'bench run',
'bench tasks' and 'bench results'. Real runs spend agent tokens; defaults use the
cheap models haiku (claude) and gpt-6-luna (codex).

Usage:
  harnez bench [flags]
  harnez bench [command]

Available Commands:
  results     Summarize recorded bench runs per condition
  run         Run bench tasks against one agent under one doc condition
  tasks       List the specced bench tasks

Flags:
  -h, --help    help for bench
      --setup   create the bench database and enable the bench commands

Use "harnez bench [command] --help" for more information about a command.

=== harnez bench results
Summarize recorded bench runs per condition

Usage:
  harnez bench results [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help         help for results
      --recent int   also list the newest N runs

=== harnez bench run
Run bench tasks against one agent under one doc condition

Usage:
  harnez bench run [flags]

Flags:
      --agent string    deprecated provider selector (use --model) (default "claude")
      --card string     with --read auto: card flags the agent is told to add to harnez read, e.g. --card=--style=compact
      --cards           deliver docs as PNG context cards instead of Markdown
      --docs string     doc variant: full or lite (default "lite")
  -h, --help            help for run
      --model string    comma-separated provider:model:tier specs from 'harnez agent models'
      --multi int[=5]   with --read: split the fixture into N files by first letter (26/N letters each); bare --multi means 5, use --multi=N otherwise
      --order string    comma-separated read task order variants: batch, sequential
  -q, --quiet           suppress preamble and progress on stderr
      --read string     comma-separated fixture read modes: native, text, auto, card
      --repeat int      runs per task (default 1)
      --repo string     repository root holding the docs (default ".")
      --task strings    task IDs to run (default: all)
      --yaml            with --read: deliver the fixture as one YAML file instead of Markdown

