=== harnez session extract
Extract all compaction summaries and real owner messages in transcript order.
Accepts a JSONL path or unique session ID prefix under ~/.claude/projects/.
Tool results, system reminders, task notifications and skill injections are removed.
Slash-command names and arguments and image placeholders are preserved.
Only Claude Code transcripts are supported. No transcript is modified.

Output includes source path/size, timestamps, counts and a truncated-tail indicator.
--json emits one JSON object with source, records and stats; default output is text.
Redirect output to a private file before reading bounded sections for a retro.
Check the exit status before consuming output: errors can leave a partial extract.

Usage:
  harnez session extract <id|path> [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for extract
      --json   emit a JSON object with source, records and stats

=== harnez skill
Manage external skills: SKILL.md directories from third-party git repositories.

install clones the repository into ~/.harnez/skills/src (or $HARNEZ_SKILLS_HOME),
pins the commit, and copies only the skill directory into the agent skill
directories that 'harnez apply' uses. Plugin hooks, MCP servers, commands, and
agents are never installed; explore lists them. Nothing from the repository is
executed.

Skills are explicit-only by default: agents use one only when you name it.
Claude Code gets the skill as a /command that never triggers on its own,
Codex gets it with implicit invocation disabled, and other agents get no copy
(they load it via 'harnez skill show'). Pass --auto to install a plain copy
that every agent may trigger on its own.

Usage:
  harnez skill [command]

Available Commands:
  explore     Show a repository's skills, scripts, required keys, and plugin extras without running anything
  install     Install one skill from a git repository into all agent skill directories
  list        List installed external skills
  remove      Remove an external skill from all agent skill directories
  search      Search installed external skills and their sibling skills in cached repositories
  show        Print an installed external skill's SKILL.md (for agents without native skills)
  update      Update external skills from their source (all when no name is given)
  vendor      Copy the config's bundled_skills from upstream into the harnez source tree

Flags:
  -c, --config string   path to config YAML file (default: embedded)
  -h, --help            help for skill

Use "harnez skill [command] --help" for more information about a command.

=== harnez skill explore
Show a repository's skills, scripts, required keys, and plugin extras without running anything

