  -h, --help            help for export

=== harnez stats
stats renders an analytical report over the tool_calls telemetry table
(internal/telemetry, issue 116, populated by 'harnez rate' and 'harnez exec'):

  - Call frequency, average score, and failure rate broken down per tool,
    per agent, and per project.
  - A global distillation byte-savings ratio (1 - distilled/raw bytes),
    computed only over rows where distillation actually ran
    (distilled_bytes IS NOT NULL).

  harnez stats
  harnez stats --tool Read --agent claude
  harnez stats --ticket harnez/120-harnez-stats-analytical-reporting --json
  harnez stats --project harnez
  harnez stats --auto
  harnez stats --agents --days 7 [--json]

--auto resolves session_id from the current environment (internal/resolve,
same resolution harnez rate/harnez exec use) and filters to just this
session's calls, instead of the all-time/all-session default.

--project filters to one project_name (issue 227) — the stable project
identity stored per tool_calls row, matching the by-project breakdown in
the report.

Filters combine with AND when more than one is given. Default output is a
formatted terminal table; --json emits the same numbers unformatted for
scripting (e.g. average score as a float, not a "2 decimal places" string).

Usage:
  harnez stats [--where] [--quality] [--json] [--strict] [--session <id> --calls] [--tool <name>] [--agent <name>] [--ticket <ticket_id>] [--project <name>] [--auto] [flags]
  harnez stats [command]

Available Commands:
  merge-legacy Merge tool calls from legacy telemetry databases into the live database

Flags:
      --agent string     filter to one agent_id
      --agents           report recent agent sessions, tokens, quota drain, and per-model totals
      --all              with --agents, show every session instead of the newest 20
      --auto             filter to the current session, resolved from the environment (like harnez rate/exec)
      --calls            list provider model requests and merged tool calls for --session
      --days int         with --agents, include sessions active in the last N days (default 7)
  -h, --help             help for stats
      --json             output the report as JSON instead of a formatted table
      --overhead         also report the harnez rate feedback overhead (issue 142): call count/bytes from telemetry plus an ESTIMATED token cost, clearly labeled as an estimate, not provider-reported
      --project string   filter to one project_name
      --quality          run read-only telemetry data-quality checks
      --session string   filter to one agent session ID
      --strict           with --quality, exit nonzero when any check warns
      --ticket string    filter to one ticket_id
      --tool string      filter to one tool_name
      --where            list harnez data stores, paths, sizes, newest records, owners, and purposes

Use "harnez stats [command] --help" for more information about a command.

=== harnez stats merge-legacy
merge-legacy copies tool_calls rows that the live database does not have yet
from legacy telemetry files, all in one transaction. The default files are the
backups the XDG move left (~/.harnez/tool_catalog.sqlite.bak-<time>); named
backups such as bak-issue331-* hold rows deleted on purpose and are only
merged when passed explicitly.
A row is already present when its created_at, session_id, agent_id, tool_name
and call_type match. Before writing, it saves a consistent copy of the live
database next to it (telemetry.sqlite.before-merge-<time>). Running it again
adds nothing.

  harnez stats merge-legacy
  harnez stats merge-legacy ~/.harnez/tool_catalog.sqlite.bak-20260927T095508.028672123Z

Usage:
  harnez stats merge-legacy [legacy.sqlite...] [flags]

Flags:
      --db string   override the telemetry database path (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/harnez/telemetry.sqlite)
  -h, --help        help for merge-legacy

=== harnez status
Show config summary and applied state

Usage:
  harnez status [flags]

Flags:
      --agy-target string     Antigravity config directory (default: agy_target from config.yaml)
      --codex-target string   Codex config.toml path (default: codex_hooks_target from config.yaml)
      --components strings    component(s) to inspect, comma-separated or repeated (e.g. docs-only,telemetry)
  -c, --config string         path to config YAML file (default: embedded)
      --debloat               show debloat-managed deny entries and toggles instead of full status (issue 316)
  -h, --help                  help for status
  -t, --target string         Claude config directory (default: ~/.claude)

=== harnez statusline
statusline reads Claude Code or Antigravity CLI statusLine JSON payloads from stdin.
For Claude Code it prints the current directory, context usage, cache-read
percentage, and rate-limit usage. With --agent agy it prints context usage,
cache-read percentage, and quota buckets.

The command is installed for Claude Code and Antigravity CLI by 'harnez apply'
when the 'usage' component and 'status_line' config.yaml key are enabled.
Codex uses its native TUI status items, configured separately by 'harnez apply'.

Usage:
  harnez statusline [flags]

Flags:
      --agent string   status payload provider: claude or agy (default "claude")
  -h, --help           help for statusline

=== harnez subagent
Stage a prompt and optional STYLE_GUIDE.png in --dir. Without a launcher,
print JSON metadata. With -- launcher args..., send the prompt on stdin and set
HARNEZ_STYLE_GUIDE to the staged image path. The launcher must support stdin prompts;
it or its agent must open/attach the PNG. This command does not itself attach images.
--doc-mode=auto uses vision for Claude/Codex and concise text for Gemini/local/unknown.
Explicit full, lite, or vision modes override provider selection.

Usage:
  harnez subagent [flags] [-- launcher args...]

Flags:
      --card string         explicit style guide PNG
  -d, --dir string          staging and launcher working directory (default ".")
      --doc-mode string     documentation mode: auto, vision, lite, full (default "auto")
  -h, --help                help for subagent
      --lite-rules string   concise rules file for lite mode
      --provider string     target profile: claude, codex, gemini, local
      --task string         task prompt

=== harnez tui
Interactive multi-model terminal chat interface for harnez.

Built on ubunatic.com/loom, providing a header status line, scrollable chat thread,
and multiline prompt box (Enter to send; Shift+Enter, Ctrl+J or Alt+Enter for a
newline). Shift+Enter and Ctrl+J need a terminal with the kitty keyboard
protocol; elsewhere they send, so use Alt+Enter or end the line with "\".
Ctrl+G edits the prompt in $VISUAL, $EDITOR or the first editor.fallbacks
entry of spec/tui.yaml found on PATH. Ctrl+O opens the active model's backend
session in the provider's own CLI (claude --resume, codex resume, agy
--conversation); the tui returns when it exits.

Prompts run through the active model's harness CLI (claude, codex, agy, pi), so
turns draw on the matching subscription; the next prompt resumes the same
backend session natively. Backend session ids are saved per --session id
(sessions.dir of spec/tui.yaml), so "harnez tui --session X" resumes them after
a restart; a session the provider no longer knows starts fresh with a note. The
header shows [resumed] or [new session] for the last turn. Esc or Ctrl+C cancels a running turn. "/model <spec>" switches
the active model (see harnez agent models). Ctrl+T (or Alt+M) or a bare "/model"
opens the model picker: models of spec/agent.yaml by provider, one row per tier,
● marks the active model and ↻ one with a backend session in this tui session.
Type to filter, up/down select, Enter switches, Esc closes; a switch during a
running turn applies to the next turn.

A prompt starting with "!" runs the rest as a background shell command (sh -c,
in the working directory) instead of sending it to the model. Ctrl+B toggles
the job panel: up/down select, Enter shows the live log, x cancels the job
(SIGTERM to its process group, SIGKILL after jobs.cancel_grace_ms), Esc closes.
Quitting cancels all running jobs.

"@" at the start of a word opens a file picker over the repository (git
ls-files, honoring .gitignore); "/" as the first character opens a command
picker with the TUI built-ins and installed skills. Type to filter, up/down
select, Tab or Enter inserts, Esc closes.

Usage:
  harnez tui [flags]

Flags:
      --cols int         column width for --render mode (default 80)
  -h, --help             help for tui
  -m, --model string     active model for tui chat session (e.g. codex:luna, claude:sonnet)
      --render           render single TUI frame to stdout and exit (for non-interactive scripts/tests)
      --rows int         row height for --render mode (default 24)
  -s, --session string   session identifier for tui chat thread

=== harnez usage
Show unified token, session, and quota status across AI coding agents

Usage:
  harnez usage [flags]
  harnez usage [command]

Aliases:
  usage, quota, tokens

Available Commands:
  archive     Copy legacy usage files into a checksummed archive
  export      Export sanitized telemetry and token-usage history as JSON for external visualization
  history     Inspect and manage recorded usage history and timelines

Flags:
      --agent string        filter to a specific agent (claude, agy, codex)
      --compact             show the compact all-usage and load panels
      --cwd string          alias for --project
  -h, --help                help for usage
      --host string         query usage from a remote host via SSH
      --interval duration   refresh interval for --watch (minimum 30s, to avoid hammering live quota APIs) (default 1m0s)
      --json                output usage in JSON format
      --loom                start usage monitor as loom app (compact view)
      --mic                 show the microphone level/recording panel in --watch (hidden if no audio interface is found)
      --minimal             show compact panels without title/status bars or hints (the default with --watch)
      --offline             read stored usage without starting the collector
  -p, --proc                show running agent processes panel in the default view / --watch
      --processes           show running agent processes panel in the default view / --watch
      --project string      attribute lifetime tokens and cost-of-change to a repository directory
  -r, --raw                 print the detailed per-field usage report instead of the selected view
      --shared              deprecated compatibility flag; local usage reads the collector store
      --splash              render startup splash while the first stored frame loads (--watch only)
      --table               show the usage table (the default for one-shot output)
  -w, --watch               refresh the stored view in place with collector age markers

Use "harnez usage [command] --help" for more information about a command.

